    "notes": "Campus at Tech oNE Crossing, just outside Kearney city limits. One record for the whole site: it already hosts a running crypto mine (Compute North ran a 30 MW facility here and planned up to 70 MW more in 2021; KSNB 2026 calls it MARA's 100 MW site), which Project Horizon will replace; the mine is decommissioned after Phase 1. Kearney City Council approved the project and its conditional use permit unanimously on 2026-09-08 (NCN). City manager: crypto mine brings the city about $2M/yr in electricity-related revenue; Phase 1 projected about $20M/yr property tax to Buffalo County, schools, CCC and the NRD. Conditions: 55 dBA average at property line, 100 ft setbacks, sound study within 90 days of operation, annual hazardous materials disclosure, start within two years. 368 MW full build-out reported by regional summaries, not confirmed in a source read. Merges leads ne-buffalo-project-horizon-kearney and ne-buffalo-mara-kearney."
